Package: qcurs
Type: Package
Title: Quality Control for Urban Temperature and Humidity Sensor Networks
Version: 0.3.4
Authors@R: person("Patrick", "Kallabis", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "patrick.kallabis@unibe.ch")
Description: Quality-control chains for urban low-cost temperature and relative
    humidity networks: temperature levels T_QC_1 to T_QC_8, humidity levels
    RH_QC_1 to RH_QC_7 (inheriting the temperature mask), each with an
    optional linear gap interpolation. Standardised input handling via
    qc_prepare_input(), documented flag codes (0 unobjected, N objected by
    level N, 50/50+N interpolated), honest refusals where the data cannot
    support a test, a per-level and per-station summary (qc_summary()), and
    corrected neighbour selection, thresholds and NA handling relative to the
    published pipeline of Amini et al. (2026), Scientific Data 13:658.
